            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of diet therapy on indices of the activity of the plasma kallikrein-kinin system of young and middle-aged ischemic heart disease patients].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Young and middle-aged patients with coronary heart disease manifested an increase in the activity of kallikrein and BAEE-esterase together with a reduction in the levels of prekallikrein and alpha 2-macroglobulin. The maximal shifts were seen in young patients and in patients who sustained myocardial infarction less than a year before examination. High kallikrein level was associated with hypertriglyceridemia and disordered fibrinolytic activity. Dietetics promoted the normalization of the disordered parameters, particularly in patients whose diet included soybean.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
